# A mail server delivering locally rewrites every address the entry accepts
# into the published one, so publishing an address the entry does not accept
# would send mail to all its other addresses somewhere nothing receives it.
ldap_create_user --domain "my_domain.tld" --uid "my_username"   \
                 --given-name "John" --surname "Smith"          \
                 --mail-alias "john.smith"                      \
                 --mail "john@my_other_domain.xyz"              \
                 --user-password "secret"

# Expected exit status: 1
# Expected error output:

Failed to create "uid=my_username,ou=users,ou=my_domain.tld,o=homelab".
This entry is associated with a local mailbox because it was created
without --mail-destination, so "john@my_other_domain.xyz" cannot be the
mail address it publishes without also being one that it accepts mail for:
  my_username@my_domain.tld
  john.smith@my_domain.tld
Add it with --mail-alias, or remove the --mail option to use the default
value of my_username@my_domain.tld for the mail attribute.

# Expected LDIF:
